Set up Project B on this Mac so it builds and its tests pass. Work out the commands
yourself; README.md in this repo has the same steps for a person. Stop and report if a
step fails in a way these notes don't cover.

What it is: a clean-sheet browser. Go managers in core/, a Vue 3 shell in shell/, a C++
adapter in engine/ on Chromium's content layer, tag 155.0.8059.41, with no patches.

The machine
- Apple silicon Mac. The full Xcode app selected with xcode-select; the command line tools
  alone can't build Chromium.
- Go 1.26 or newer, Node 22 or newer, Python 3. Homebrew is fine.
- About 150 GB free: the Chromium source is about 60 GB, a build output about as much again.

Steps, in order, each with how to know it worked
1. The repo at ~/Official/workspace/ulaa/project-b. tools/build.sh, package.sh and
   release.sh have that path written in for now, so clone it there.
2. npm install in shell/.
3. tools/fetch-chromium.sh. Long download. Done when it prints RESULT=ok and
   chromium/src is checked out at tag 155.0.8059.41.
4. tools/build.sh. Done when it prints RESULT=ok and chromium/src/out/pb/project_b exists.
   The first build is a full Chromium build: about an hour on 32 cores, several hours on a
   laptop. Run it in the background and wait for it once; don't poll in a tight loop.
5. Test tools, outside the repo for now:
   - Playwright under ~/.local/playwright (npm install playwright there, then install its
     Chromium). shell/e2e/*.cjs load it from that path.
   - ChromeDriver 155.0.8059.41 for mac-arm64 from Chrome for Testing, unzipped so the
     binary is ~/PW_TOOLS/chromedriver/chromedriver-mac-arm64/chromedriver. The
     CHROMEDRIVER environment variable can point elsewhere.
6. Run, from the repo, and expect each to end with "all passed":
   (cd core && go test ./...)          # ends with ok lines, no FAIL
   node shell/e2e/first-app.cjs
   node shell/e2e/settings.cjs
   python3 tools/drive_first_app.py
   python3 tools/drive_first_app.py settings
   python3 tools/drive_chromedriver.py
7. Report each command's result, with any FAIL lines in full.

Known traps
- The real-app tests start the app themselves; don't start it first. If an earlier run
  left project_b processes behind, stop only those you started.
- tools/check_first_paint.py needs a logged-in, unlocked screen and a screen-capture tool
  with Screen Recording permission. Without them it prints "skipped"; that is not a failure.
- Real clicks, drags and full screen need the macOS VM in tools/vm (docs/vm-testing.md).
  Not part of this setup.
- Packaging and releases need the signing key, which isn't on a fresh machine. Not part of
  this setup.
- Don't edit Chromium's source; the project builds it unpatched.
